.Dd May 3, 2026
.Dt CRATE-HUB 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm crate-hub
.Nd central aggregator for multi-host crate(8) deployments
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl f
.Op Fl c Ar config
.Op Fl p Ar port
.Op Fl w Ar webdir
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
polls
.Xr crated 8
instances on a list of remote nodes, caches their state in a
SQLite store, and serves an aggregated REST API plus an embedded
web dashboard. It is the single pane of glass for an operator
running containers on multiple hosts.
.Pp
The hub itself does not proxy mutating requests
.Po
.Ic POST
to start/stop/restart a container, etc.
.Pc :
the dashboard hits each node's
.Xr crated 8
directly so the
.Em admin
Bearer token never leaves the operator's browser. The hub is
read-mostly aggregator.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f , Fl Fl foreground
Stay in the foreground; do not fork.
.It Fl c Ar config , Fl Fl config Ar config
Path to the YAML configuration file. Default
.Pa /usr/local/etc/crate-hub.conf .
.It Fl p Ar port , Fl Fl port Ar port
TCP port to listen on. Default
.Ar 9810
.Pq or Va listen_port in the configuration file .
.It Fl b Ar address , Fl Fl bind Ar address
Address to listen on. Default
.Ar 127.0.0.1
.Pq or Va listen_host in the configuration file .
See
.Sx SECURITY
before binding to a routable address.
.It Fl w Ar webdir , Fl Fl webdir Ar webdir
Directory served as the embedded dashboard. Default
.Pa /usr/local/share/crate-hub/web .
.El
.Pp
.Nm Cm schedule
.Op Ar args
runs the placement recommendation once and prints it
.Pq same logic as Pa /api/v1/scheduling/least-loaded .
.Sh ENDPOINTS
.Bl -tag -width "POST /api/v1/admin/prune                  "
.It GET Pa /healthz
Liveness check.
.It GET Pa /api/v1/nodes
List configured nodes with their last-poll reachability and
last-error string.
.It GET Pa /api/v1/nodes/:host/containers
Container list reported by a specific node.
.It GET Pa /api/v1/containers
All containers across all nodes, grouped by node.
.It GET Pa /api/v1/aggregate
Single-shot summary for the dashboard banner: nodes total /
reachable / down, containers total.
.It GET Pa /api/v1/datacenters
Per-datacenter summary: nodes total / reachable / down, containers.
.It GET Pa /api/v1/ha/orders
HA failover orders derived from the node reachability streaks and
the
.Va ha:
section; the hub never executes them itself.
.It GET Pa /api/v1/scheduling/least-loaded Op ?current=node
Placement recommendation for the next container.
.It GET Pa /metrics
Prometheus exposition aggregating all nodes.
.It POST Pa /api/v1/admin/prune
Drop store entries older than 48 hours.
Accepted from loopback only.
.El
.Pp
Node entries in
.Pa /api/v1/nodes
and
.Pa /api/v1/containers
carry
.Va stale: true
when the last poll failed and the container list shown is the previous
good snapshot.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
.Bd -literal -offset indent
listen_host: 127.0.0.1     # -b / --bind overrides
listen_port: 9810          # -p / --port overrides

# Polling interval for each node, seconds.
poll_interval: 15

nodes:
  - name:  alpha
    host:  alpha.example.com:9800   # or host: + port:; IPv6 as [fd00::5]:9800
    token: <admin-token-for-alpha>
    datacenter: eu-1
  - name:  beta
    host:  beta.example.com
    port:  9800
    token: <admin-token-for-beta>
    tls:   true                     # HTTPS to a crated with a server certificate
    ca_cert: /usr/local/etc/ssl/crate-ca.pem
    # tls_cert / tls_key: client certificate for mTLS (implies tls: true)

ha:
  threshold_seconds: 60
  specs:
    - container: web
      primary: alpha
      partners: [beta]
.Ed
.Pp
The node's server certificate is always verified when TLS is used
.Pq against Va ca_cert when set, else the system store .
Without
.Va tls
the admin token travels in cleartext; keep such nodes on a trusted
network.
.Sh SECURITY
The hub API has no authentication of its own.
It binds to
.Ar 127.0.0.1
by default; to serve a dashboard to other hosts put an authenticating
TLS reverse proxy in front of it, or bind to a network that only
trusted operators can reach.
.Pa /api/v1/nodes
exposes node host:port values and last-error strings;
.Pa /api/v1/admin/prune
is accepted from loopback only.
Dashboard start/stop/restart/destroy buttons talk to the node daemons
directly with the admin token stored in the browser, so each
.Xr crated 8
must be reachable from the browser and permit the hub's origin.
.Sh WEB DASHBOARD
The
.Pa /usr/local/share/crate-hub/web
directory ships
.Pa index.html ,
.Pa app.js ,
and
.Pa style.css .
The page polls
.Pa /api/v1/aggregate ,
.Pa /api/v1/datacenters ,
.Pa /api/v1/nodes ,
and
.Pa /api/v1/containers
every five seconds. Mutating actions
.Pq Ic start , Ic stop , Ic restart , Ic destroy
hit the per-node
.Xr crated 8
directly via
.Ic fetch ;
the operator pastes an admin Bearer token on first use and the
browser keeps it in
.Ar localStorage .
.Pp
This embedded dashboard is intentionally minimal — node + container
visibility, datacenter rollups, and one-click lifecycle buttons.
A full datacenter administration UI
.Pq DC create/rename, drag-drop node moves, per-DC quotas,
.Pq attached logs/console
will live in its own repository so the frontend can pick its own
framework and release cadence independent of the C++ daemons.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/local/share/crate-hub/web/index.html"
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/crate-hub.conf
Operator-edited config file.
.It Pa /var/db/crate-hub/metrics.db
SQLite store of polled metrics.
.It Pa /usr/local/share/crate-hub/web/index.html
Embedded dashboard root.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr crate 5 ,
.Xr crated 8 ,
.Xr jls 8
